The XvjzMC project aims to provide a secure and stable Minecraft server experience. However, like any software, vulnerabilities may exist. Here’s some guidance and information:

- Reporting Vulnerabilities: If you discover a security issue, please report it by creating an [issue on GitHub](https://github.com/SparkleSavvy/XvjzMC/issues) labeled "Security".
- Project Branches:
  - Alpha and Beta: These branches are for testing and experimentation. No technical support is provided for these branches. Use them at your own risk.
  - Release: The stable version with full technical support. Security updates and bug fixes are prioritized for this branch.
- Recommendations: Regularly update your server and plugins to the latest versions to minimize risks.

